  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Heparin is an anticoagulant (blood thinner) used to treat and prevent blood clots, including pulmonary embolism, and is also used in antiphospholipid syndrome. It is a widely used medicine and appears on the WHO list of essential medicines.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q190016&quot;>Wikidata Q190016</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>heparin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>B01AB01, C05BA03, S01XA14</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01109&quot;>DB01109</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:28304&quot;>28304</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q190016&quot;>Q190016</a></td></tr></table></body></html>"));
